A||||10||GWMORGAN||1st, 2nd And Reverse.........||||8||
Z||000000||GWMORGAN||12-21-1999||10:16 PM||||At the end of clutch travel (pressing down), there's a clicking sound and now it's hard to select 1st and 2nd gears (no grinding), and reverse (big grinding).The fluid in the clutch system has turned black. (1) Could it be time to rebuild/replace the master or (2) is it the clutch going south? Once in gear, she runs as strong as ever. Thanks for info.<P><BR>86GT 5spd. with steel pedal.||||reg||8
Z||000001||JetroGT||12-22-1999||04:50 AM||||It could be that the oil in the tranny is low or leaking. The 88's manual tranny had the stick to check this. On the 86 I think you have to unbolt a plug. Some one correct me if I'm wrong on this. ||||reg||1
Z||000002||Carrolles||12-22-1999||06:52 AM||||Check the alignment of your shifter cables.  The procedure is in most of the manuals.<P>Do you have the same trouble shifitng into these gears when the engine is not running?  If not then you are probable getting close to needing a master cylinder repair/replacement.  Usually when you replace/rebuild the master cylinder the slave fails soon after so you might be getting prepared for that.<P>Do you find that the pedal is closer to the floor at clutch disengagement lately?||||reg||1
Z||000003||GWMORGAN||12-22-1999||07:28 AM||||JetroGT.....The tranny was drained and refilled with 5w-30 syntec. oil about a month ago.<P><BR>Carrolles......The shifter cables were realigned and I can easily shift into gears wiyh the enging off. To make it easier,I shift into gear before I start her up. My clutch pedal is at the maximum height possible.<P>I'm suspecting master cylinder rebuild/replacement. What's the easiest method of removing the master cylinder? Thanks for info guys.<P>Another note...Merry Christmas and Best Wishes For The Year 2000 And Those To Come!!||||reg||1
Z||000004||William Federle||12-22-1999||02:29 PM||||When I had my clutch problems, I bled the slave over and over. The tip off of 1/2 of<BR>the basic problem was that if the clutch was<BR>held in, and you observed the slave, it would<BR>slowly creep back from its extended position<BR>(and it only traveled about 3/4"). I got a<BR>suggestion from a friend that the fluid must be leaking past the seal in the master. I replaced the master and got what you already have - a steel clutch pedal  (the second half of my problem) and that solved<BR>my problems so far. Also my slave cylinder travel is now about 1-1/8".One other thing, I still grind sometimes when shifting into reverse but I can always prevent that, I've found, by shifting into third, and then into reverse.<BR>good luck.<P><BR>[This message has been edited by William Federle (edited 12-22-1999).]<p>[This message has been edited by William Federle (edited 12-22-1999).]||||reg||1
Z||000005||william_thorniii||12-22-1999||05:50 PM||||William, <P>The grinding in reverse is most likely due to bad synchros.  By shifting into 3rd, you are aligning the gears and then you do not grind going into Reverse.  <P>William T. Thorn, III||||reg||10
Z||000006||Patrick||12-22-1999||06:46 PM||||<BR>Bad synchros on <B>reverse</B> gear??<P>Any Muncie or Borg Warner tranny I ever had apart did not have any synchros on reverse gear.||||reg||5
Z||000007||Monkeyman||12-22-1999||06:53 PM||||The last tranny I had in a big truck was an 18 spd overdrive (no synchros in a big truck) and it was easier to shift into reverse if you shifted into 1st gear first (1st gear is just behind reverse in a semi).||||reg||1
Z||000008||william_thorniii||12-22-1999||07:09 PM||||OOOOOPS!  Pat you are right, there aren't any synchros on the Reverse gear.  I am at work, and everybody knows that ones brain doesn't function when at work..<P>William T. Thorn, III||||reg||10
Z||000009||Patrick||12-22-1999||08:46 PM||||<BR>Hey, as long as it's functioning when you're behind the wheel... <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">||||reg||14
Z||000010||GWMORGAN||12-22-1999||09:44 PM||||I had someone hold the pedal to the floor and observed the slave cylinder piston...It did retract a bit so I'll be rebuilding master and slave cylinders. <BR>Thanks for helping out guys,I've saved a lot of dough because of this forum and a BIG THANKS to Cliff for making it possible.||||reg||1
